.TH MASTOTEST 1
.SH NAME
mastotest \- test masto(1)'s decoders and network paths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mastotest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Mastotest
calls
.IR masto (1)'s
own in-process test seams, the same pattern
.IR bskytest (1)
uses against Bluesky: no credentials file, no network mocking.
Offline seams run first, over hand-built fixtures in each endpoint's
real response shape:
.TP
.B htmltest
the HTML stripper and entity decoder, table-driven (the seam that
originally caught the
.BR <br> /\c
.B </p>
word-gluing bug and the quoted-\c
.B >
markup leak);
.TP
.B feedtest
the timeline walk: account/content fallbacks, entity decoding
composed with the stripper, a boost naming both accounts, ordering,
the
.B -v
id lines, and
.B -max
paging-id extraction;
.TP
.B notiftest
the notifications walk (auth-only endpoint, so offline is the only
leg);
.TP
.B profiletest
profile fields, note stripping, counts;
.TP
.B contexttest
a hand-built thread: ancestor, marked subject, indented descendant;
.TP
.B buildtest
the status-posting request bodies, pinned byte for byte.
.PP
The live seams then hit real
.B mastodon.social
endpoints:
.TP
.B pubtest
the public instance description;
.TP
.B lookuptest
account lookup \(em the same path
.B follow
uses \(em decoded by the same
.B profiledecode
the offline seam pinned;
.TP
.B livecontexttest
a real conversation (the Mastodon project account's newest status
and its context) through
.BR contextdecode ;
.TP
.B authposttest
a status POST with a bogus token, which must draw the server's own
decoded error through the full authenticated-POST path without
posting anything anywhere.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/mastotest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR masto (1),
.IR bskytest (1),
.IR httpstest (1),
.IR https (2)
.SH BUGS
The live legs need the real network; a failure there can mean the
world changed rather than the code. Nothing here (deliberately)
posts, favourites, boosts or follows for real \(em see
.IR masto (1)'s
own BUGS.
